# Combobox

A searchable select: a trigger button opening a filterable listbox,
with the choice submitted via a hidden input.

<%= embed :combobox, :default %>

## When to use

- One choice from a long list: clinicians, clinics, medications.
- One choice from an unfamiliar list, where the user finds by typing
  rather than scanning.

## When not to use

- Few, familiar options — `radio_group` (≤5) or native `select`.
- Free text that happens to have suggestions — that is an `input`;
  a combobox only submits listed values.
- Commands/navigation — `command` is the menu-shaped sibling.

## Usage

`render_combobox` (`Gesso::Components::ComboboxHelper`) resolves the selected
label and renders the searchable select; behaviour comes from basecoat's
vendored `select.js`, and the selection is tracked in a hidden input for
normal form submission.

```erb
<%%= render_combobox(
  name: "clinician",
  selected: @episode.clinician_id,
  placeholder: "Select clinician",
  options: clinicians.map { |c| { value: c.id, label: c.name } }
) %>
```

| Param | Default | Notes |
| ----- | ------- | ----- |
| `name` | — | hidden input name |
| `options` | `[]` | `{ value:, label: }` hashes |
| `selected` | — | pre-selected value |
| `placeholder` | `"Select…"` | trigger label when empty |
| `searchable` | `true` | `false` drops the filter for short lists |
| `id` | — | id for the hidden input |

The check mark on the selected option is CSS-driven from
`aria-selected` — no extra markup.

## Do and don't

- Do give `placeholder` the field's noun ("Select clinician"), not
  generic "Select…", when the label alone is ambiguous.
- Do use `searchable: false` for a short list that still wants the
  combobox visual — but first ask whether `select` or `radio_group`
  fits better.
- Don't load enormous option lists into the page for client-side
  filtering; past a few hundred options the lookup belongs
  server-side (the patient search pattern).
- Don't use a combobox where multiple values are needed — it tracks
  one selection.

## Accessibility and content

- Trigger is a real `<button>`; the popover list is
  `role="listbox"` with `aria-selected` on options and the filter
  input wired as `role="combobox"` — keyboard and screen-reader
  flows come from the basecoat pattern.
- Option labels match what users would type — search filters on the
  visible label.
